--[[
  `add(code, strings)` adds a language. The strings must fit the shape
  of the base, so a key that the language lacks is a type error at the
  call, in the editor and under `alloy flux`.

  A key that the code reads and the base lacks is a type error too. A
  misspelled key does not reach the game as an empty label.
]]

import { Gloss } from '@packages/gloss'
import en from './lang/en.toml'
import fr from './lang/fr.toml'
import ja from './lang/ja.toml'
import ru from './lang/ru.toml'

const lang = new Gloss('en', en)

-- Each of these has every key of `en.toml`.
lang:add('fr', fr)
lang:add('ru', ru)
lang:add('ja', ja)

print(lang.t.quest.title)

--[[
  Take `sold_out` out of `fr.toml`, and the `add` call does not
  compile. The message names the table where the key is missing:

    error(luau): TypeError: Expected this to be '{ read language: ...,
      read shop: { read buy: string, read sold_out: string, read title:
      string } }' but got '{ language: ..., shop: { buy: string, title:
      string } }'; accessing `shop` results in `{ buy: string, title:
      string }` in the latter type and `{ read buy: string, read
      sold_out: string, read title: string }` in the former type

  Read a key that is not there, and that does not compile either:

    print(lang.t.shop.titel)
    error(luau): TypeError: Key 'titel' not found in table
      '{ read buy: string, read sold_out: string, read title: string }'

  What Luau checks, and what it does not:

  - A missing key is an error, at each depth.
  - An extra key is not: Luau takes a table with more keys where it asks
    for fewer. `lang:check()` lists extra keys (step 020).
  - A plural table may hold other forms than the base. Russian adds
    `few` and `many`, and Japanese has `other` alone (step 004).
  - The text of a string is not in its type, so a placeholder that
    differs is not a type error. `lang:check()` compares them.
  - An array, such as a list of tips, keeps the type of the base, and
    its items must match it exactly.
  - A key in a variable, `t.items[id]`, does not type check: Luau does
    not index a table type with a string. The shop example gives each
    item a function that reads its key.
  - `alloy check` runs no Luau type check. Run `alloy flux`.
]]
